    <briefdescription>
<para>Nelson-Siegel fitting method. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fits a discount function to the form <formula id="398">$ d(t) = \exp^{-r t}, $</formula> where the zero rate <formula id="399">$r$</formula> is defined as <formula id="400">\[ r \equiv c_0 + (c_0 + c_1)*(1 - exp^{-\kappa*t}/(\kappa t) - c_2 exp^{ - \kappa t}. \]</formula> See: Nelson, C. and A. Siegel (1985): &quot;Parsimonious modeling of yield
       curves for US Treasury bills.&quot; NBER Working Paper Series, no 1594. </para>    </detaileddescription>
    <location file="C:/Develop/QuantLib-1.2.1/ql/termstructures/yield/nonlinearfittingmethods.hpp" line="67" bodyfile="C:/Develop/QuantLib-1.2.1/ql/termstructures/yield/nonlinearfittingmethods.hpp" bodystart="66" bodyend="74"/>
